## Why This Is Asked
This probes practical Azure Policy usage, Private Endpoints, tagging discipline, and CI/CD gating with rollback in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access for storage accounts
- Private Endpoints and private DNS configuration
- Resource tagging as policy gates in CI/CD
- Rollback to last known-good ARM/Bicep template
- Monitoring and alerting via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```json
{
  "properties": {
    "displayName": "Deny public network access on storage accounts",
    "policyType": "Regular",
    "mode": "All",
    "policyRule": {
      "if": {
        "allOf": [
          {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
          {"field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/networkAcls/defaultAction", "equals": "Allow"}
        ]
      },
      "then": {"effect": "Deny"}
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for multi-region storage and cross-tenant sharing?
- How would you test the CI gate to minimize false positives and ensure rollback works?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess hands-on orchestration across Azure components during incidents, focusing on tenant isolation, automated rollback safety, and auditable controls.

## Key Concepts
- UEBA-driven automation (Defender for Cloud/Sentinel)
- Per-tenant network isolation (NSG, Private Endpoint)
- Key Vault key rotation and re-encryption
- Token revocation and Conditional Access control
- Canary-based rollback mechanisms
- Centralized auditing and alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator snippet
async function quarantineTenant(tenantId){
  await applyPerTenantNSG(tenantId);
  await rotateKeyVaultKeys(tenantId);
  await revokeTokensAndDisableCA(tenantId);
  await rollbackToLastGoodRelease(tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to design a scalable, auditable cross-tenant security workflow with concrete automation points across DevOps, container registries, policy enforcement, and cross-tenant governance.

## Key Concepts

- Artifact signing and image provenance verification
- Azure Container Registry content trust implementation
- Azure Policy enforcement for supply-chain controls
- Azure Lighthouse cross-tenant approval workflows
- Immutable tagging strategies and automated rollback capabilities

## Code Example

```json
{
  "policyDefinition": {
    "name": "RequireSignedImages",
    "properties": {
      "description": "Enforces signed container images for AKS deployments",
      "policyRule": {
        "if": {
          "field": "type",
          "equals": "Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters"
        },
        "then": {
          "effect": "deny",
          "details": [
            {
              "field": "Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/addonProfiles.omsagent.enabled",
              "equals": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
